  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Public Sector Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the programme is to support the Ugandan government&apos;s efforts to improve the administration of the public sector in order to increase capacity for providing service to the poorest part of the population in an efficient, transparent and responsible manner. If the reforms are implemented with success the programme&#xbf;s approach could be repeated other places in the state. The programme consisted of three components: 1) Strengthening the overall strategically coordination in the Ugandan state ministry, including a special focus on the strengthening of the sector working group that is in control of budgets and perform transversal coordination; 2) Support to reform of the public sector in preparation of better and inexpensive deliverance of main services (health, water, education etc.), and; 3) Support to the local governments, who are primary delivers of services to the country&#xbf;s poor. Approximately a third of the state budget and nearly three quarters of the public services is administrated by the local governments.</narrative>
  </description>
